{
 "@context": {
  "dcterms": "http://purl.org/dc/terms/",
  "owl": "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#",
  "prov": "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#",
  "rdf": "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#",
  "rdfs": "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#",
  "schema": "https://schema.org/",
  "skos": "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#",
  "wd": "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/",
  "wg": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/",
  "wgo": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#",
  "xsd": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
 },
 "@graph": [
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/acceptance/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I fighting a feeling I'm entitled to have, or criticising myself for having it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:acceptance"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/acceptance/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is this situation truly fixed, or am I calling it unchangeable so I don't have to act?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:acceptance"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/acceptance/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I accepting what happened, or am I approving of it or giving up?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:acceptance"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/acceptance/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Once I've let this be, what is the one step that still matters most?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:acceptance"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/acceptance/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I'm anxious and a bit hurt, and that makes sense the week before a launch. The departure is settled. What's still open is the handover and which features we cut, so that's where this afternoon goes.",
   "wgo:before": "I shouldn't be this rattled; I'm the lead. I'll push the worry down, tell everyone it's fine, and keep reopening the decision to let her go in my head all weekend.",
   "wgo:situation": "A week before a product launch, a team lead learns that a key engineer is leaving and the launch date cannot move.",
   "wgo:why": "The wiser response stops spending effort on fighting the feeling and the fact, which leaves attention free for the parts of the situation that can still be shaped; it accepts the departure without giving up on the launch."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/adversity/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I adding a \"second arrow\" of blame, catastrophe or self-pity to the pain this situation actually brings?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:adversity"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/adversity/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Which parts of this are up to me right now, and which are not?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:adversity"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/adversity/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "When I look back on this, am I trying to understand what happened and what it taught me, or only to tie it up neatly?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:adversity"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/adversity/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is the load more than I can carry alone, so that it is time to lean on others or talk to a professional?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:adversity"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/adversity/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "This really hurts, and I don't have to pretend otherwise. I can't change the decision, but I can update my CV, talk to two mentors this week and tell my partner how I'm feeling. In a few months I'll look back at what I'd do differently, not just at how to feel better about it.",
   "wgo:before": "This is a disaster and it's unfair. I'll replay every meeting tonight to find who's to blame, and tell everyone I'm totally fine.",
   "wgo:situation": "A team lead learns that the product she spent two years building is being cancelled and her role will end in three months.",
   "wgo:why": "Separating the loss itself from the stories piled on top of it, acting on what is still controllable and leaning on others protects judgment, and open, exploratory reflection afterwards is the kind linked to wisdom."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/after-action-review/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I looking at what happened in order to learn from it, or to find someone to blame, including myself?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:after-action-review"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/after-action-review/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I heard how this looked to the other people involved before deciding why it went the way it did?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:after-action-review"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/after-action-review/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Did I ask what went right and why, or only what went wrong?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:after-action-review"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/after-action-review/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What is the one concrete thing I will do differently next time, and when will I check that I did it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:after-action-review"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/after-action-review/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "The manager books thirty minutes the next morning, says the aim is to learn rather than to find fault, and asks what the plan was, what actually happened and why. The team notices that the scope was settled late and the pricing was never reviewed, also notes that the client praised the case studies, and agrees that next time pricing gets a review two days before the deadline, with one person responsible.",
   "wgo:before": "The manager sends a one-line message blaming the client's budget, the team moves straight to the next bid, and nobody mentions that the pricing section was finished in a rush on the last night.",
   "wgo:situation": "A small team's bid for a client contract has just been turned down, two weeks after an intense push to finish the proposal.",
   "wgo:why": "A specific, blame-free look at both what worked and what failed turns a disappointment into a lesson the team will actually use, instead of a convenient external excuse or a quiet repeat of the same mistake."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/after-action-review/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "After-action review",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/after-action-review/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/after-action-review/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/after-action-review/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/after-action-review/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/after-action-review/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/after-action-review/howto/6"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/after-action-review/howto/7"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/after-action-review/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Hold the review soon after the event, while memories are fresh, and keep it short; for a long project, review at each milestone rather than only at the end."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/after-action-review/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Agree at the start that the purpose is learning, not grading or blame, and that what is said will not be used to punish anyone."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/after-action-review/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Establish what was supposed to happen, using the original plan, goals or standards."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/after-action-review/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Reconstruct what actually happened from several viewpoints and from any objective records, before anyone explains or defends."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/after-action-review/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Ask why the gap opened, looking for specific causes you could influence, including your own decisions."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/after-action-review/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Review what went well and why, not only what went wrong."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/after-action-review/howto/7",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 7,
   "schema:text": "Agree on one to three concrete things to sustain or change, name who will apply each, and check at the start of the next similar task that they were applied."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/amor-fati/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I spending my energy wishing this had not happened, or deciding what to make of the fact that it did?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:amor-fati"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/amor-fati/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I calling something \"fate\" to avoid changing what I could and should still change?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:amor-fati"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/amor-fati/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Could I tell the story of this setback as part of a life I would still choose to live again?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:amor-fati"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/amor-fati/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "It happened, and it is now part of my story and the team's. What did these months teach us, and what can we carry into the next thing? I'll grieve it honestly, then decide what to build from it.",
   "wgo:before": "This should never have happened. I keep replaying the meeting where it was killed and resenting everyone in it, and I've stopped caring about the next project.",
   "wgo:situation": "A project manager's carefully planned product launch is cancelled after a reorganisation, and months of her team's work will never ship.",
   "wgo:why": "The wiser response neither pretends the loss was good nor fights the fact that it occurred; it takes the event as given and asks what a life that includes it can become."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Whose interests have I left off the list, including people who are not in the room?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:balance-theory-of-wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Would this choice still look good to me a year from now, not just this week?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:balance-theory-of-wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I adapting, trying to change things, or walking away, and is that the right response here?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:balance-theory-of-wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is the common good I am appealing to one the other people affected would recognise, or just my own preference dressed up?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:balance-theory-of-wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I want this project, the junior colleague needs support, and the client needs the deliverable. Can I ask for a one-week start date, pair them with a senior for three days, and take the project after?",
   "wgo:before": "This is my shot. Take the project, reassign the work tonight and let the junior person sort themselves out.",
   "wgo:situation": "A team lead is offered a high-profile project that would mean handing a struggling junior colleague's half-finished work to someone else three days before the client deadline.",
   "wgo:why": "The first answer serves only one interest in the short term; the second looks for an option that balances personal, interpersonal and wider interests over a longer horizon, which is what Sternberg means by a wise solution."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Balance theory of wisdom",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/5"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Name the decision and the outcome you are tempted to choose before you start weighing it."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "List the interests at stake on three levels - yours, those of the specific people around you, and those of the wider team, community or environment."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "For each option, write down who gains and who pays in the next few weeks and in a few years."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Ask whether to adapt to the situation, try to change it, or leave it for a better one, and why."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Choose the option that best serves a common good you could defend out loud to everyone affected, and say which value settled the trade-off."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/berlin-wisdom-paradigm/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I considered how this problem looks across the person's whole life, past and future, and not only today?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:berlin-wisdom-paradigm"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/berlin-wisdom-paradigm/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I named what I do not know about this situation, and what I would do if things turn out differently than I expect?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:berlin-wisdom-paradigm"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/berlin-wisdom-paradigm/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I judging this choice by my own values only, or have I tried to understand the values and priorities behind it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:berlin-wisdom-paradigm"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/bhagavad-gita/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I doing this because it is the right thing for me to do here, or only for what I hope to get from it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:bhagavad-gita"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/bhagavad-gita/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "If the result goes against me, will I still be able to say I acted well?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:bhagavad-gita"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/bhagavad-gita/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is my calm steadiness, or have I quietly stopped caring about the people my action affects?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:bhagavad-gita"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/bhagavad-gita/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "My part is to make this proposal as sound and honest as I can, including the analysis they might question. I want a yes, but I'll judge my work by whether I did it well, not only by what the board decides.",
   "wgo:before": "Everything depends on their yes. I'll cut the risky analysis they might question, and if they say no, the whole year was wasted.",
   "wgo:situation": "A project lead has spent months on a proposal that goes to a review board next week, and a promotion may ride on the board's verdict.",
   "wgo:why": "The wiser response keeps caring about the outcome while letting the quality of the action, which is in your hands, guide what you do, which is close to what the Gita's teaching on the fruits of action asks."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Would going without this actually cause me pain, or would I just feel I had fallen behind someone?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:classification-of-desires"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Does this desire have a natural stopping point, or would more always seem better?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:classification-of-desires"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What am I already giving up, in time, health or peace, to chase it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:classification-of-desires"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "Which of these would actually hurt to go without? We need more space for the kids, so that's real. The car and the title are mostly about how I look next to others, and I can drop them if they cost my evenings.",
   "wgo:before": "Everyone at my level has these things. Once I have them I'll finally be able to relax.",
   "wgo:situation": "After a good year, a project manager starts eyeing a bigger house, a premium car and a more senior title, and finds herself working weekends and sleeping badly to get all three.",
   "wgo:why": "Sorting the wants separates a real need from desires driven by comparison, so effort goes where it buys security and the rest stops dictating her time."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-defusion/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I treating this thought as a fact about the world, or as something my mind is saying right now?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:cognitive-defusion"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-defusion/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is this thought helping me act on what matters here, or just making me want to escape?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:cognitive-defusion"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-defusion/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I using a defusion trick to make the feeling go away, rather than to make room for it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:cognitive-defusion"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-defusion/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I checked whether the thought is pointing to a real problem that deserves action?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:cognitive-defusion"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-defusion/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I'm having the thought that they'll see I'm out of my depth. That's the old not-good-enough story turning up before a big meeting, as it usually does. It can come along; I'll still make the recommendation I believe in and take the questions.",
   "wgo:before": "It's true, I'm out of my depth. I'll trim the proposal to the safe parts, skip the risky recommendation and read straight from the slides so nobody can ask me anything.",
   "wgo:situation": "Ten minutes before presenting a proposal to senior leaders, a manager keeps hearing the thought \"they're going to see I'm out of my depth\".",
   "wgo:why": "The wiser response neither obeys the thought nor wastes the last ten minutes trying to argue it away; seeing it as a familiar mental event leaves the manager free to act on the judgement they actually hold."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-defusion/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Cognitive defusion",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-defusion/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-defusion/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-defusion/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-defusion/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-defusion/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-defusion/howto/6"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-defusion/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Notice when a thought is steering you, especially a harsh verdict about yourself or a prediction of disaster that you are treating as plain fact."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-defusion/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Name it as a thought by restating it as \"I'm having the thought that…\", or label its kind, such as \"the not-good-enough story\" or \"a prediction\"."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-defusion/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Loosen its literal hold for a few seconds by saying its key word aloud quickly and repeatedly, or saying the sentence very slowly or in a silly voice, until it sounds more like sounds than a message."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-defusion/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Let it stay without arguing with it, proving it wrong or pushing it away; acknowledge it, for example by thanking your mind for the warning."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-defusion/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Ask what you would do next if this thought were just background noise, and take that step while the thought comes along."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-defusion/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Stop and seek professional support if a thought is overwhelming, persistent or about harming yourself; defusion is a self-help skill, not crisis care."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-reappraisal/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is this something I can still change, so that I should act rather than reinterpret?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:cognitive-reappraisal"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-reappraisal/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is my new reading of the situation true, or just comfortable?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:cognitive-reappraisal"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-reappraisal/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I using a reframe to talk myself out of a feeling that is telling me something important, such as that I'm being treated unfairly?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:cognitive-reappraisal"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-reappraisal/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Did the reframe actually change how I feel, or do I need a different approach?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:cognitive-reappraisal"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-reappraisal/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "This stings, and it's a real setback. What do I actually know? They rejected this version, not the team. Some of it I can still change: I'll ask for their reasons tomorrow. The part I can't change I'll treat as one lost bid in a long year, not a verdict on us.",
   "wgo:before": "This is a disaster and it proves I'm not good at this. I'll just smile, say it's fine, and stew about it tonight.",
   "wgo:situation": "A project lead learns in a meeting that the client has rejected the proposal their team spent three weeks on.",
   "wgo:why": "The wiser response keeps the feeling honest, uses reappraisal on the part that can't be changed, and keeps the frustration that should drive action on the part that can, instead of masking everything and ruminating later."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-reappraisal/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Cognitive reappraisal",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-reappraisal/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-reappraisal/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-reappraisal/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-reappraisal/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-reappraisal/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-reappraisal/howto/6"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-reappraisal/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Name the feeling and the specific thought driving it, for example \"I'm anxious because I think this mistake will get me fired.\""
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-reappraisal/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Ask whether you can still change the situation itself; if you can, plan that action first and use reappraisal only to steady yourself enough to act."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-reappraisal/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Test the interpretation against the facts, as you would a colleague's claim, and look for what you actually know versus what you are assuming."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-reappraisal/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Try one or two alternative readings that are also true, such as what the event will matter in a year, what you can still influence, or how a neutral observer would describe it."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-reappraisal/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Pick the reading you can honestly believe, not the most comforting one, and let it guide your next step."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-reappraisal/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "After a while, check whether the feeling has shifted; if the reframe isn't landing, switch to another strategy such as acceptance, talking it through or taking a break."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/common-wisdom-model/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What do I not know about this situation, and how might the facts change what I think?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:common-wisdom-model"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/common-wisdom-model/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Whose perspective have I not yet considered, and what would this look like from where they stand?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:common-wisdom-model"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/common-wisdom-model/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is there a way forward that serves both my interests and theirs, rather than one at the other's expense?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:common-wisdom-model"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/common-wisdom-model/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I aiming at what is true and fair here, or only at winning the point?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:common-wisdom-model"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I actually noticed what this person is going through, or only what their trouble costs me?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:compassion"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I acting to ease their suffering, or to escape my own discomfort at seeing it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:compassion"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is my concern shaded by a quiet judgement that they brought this on themselves, or that I am above them?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:compassion"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Would I feel and act the same way if the people suffering were many, distant or unlike me?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:compassion"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I stop and take it in: 'That's a hard week. What would help most right now?' I move the deadline with the client myself, ask whether they want work taken off them or kept as a distraction, and agree a check-in for next week so the rest of the team isn't left guessing.",
   "wgo:before": "I either brush past it ('sorry to hear that, but the client is furious, I need it by tomorrow') or I am so upset for them that I quietly redo the work myself at midnight and never mention the deadline again.",
   "wgo:situation": "A reliable team member misses a client deadline and, when you ask about it, mentions that a parent was taken into hospital last week.",
   "wgo:why": "Compassion notices the suffering and is moved by it, but it also stays steady enough to choose help that fits this person and stays fair to everyone else involved."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I wishing this person well, or am I telling myself that what they did was fine?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:compassionate-reappraisal"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is this wrong still going on and within my power to change, so that action rather than reappraisal is the priority?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:compassionate-reappraisal"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "After the exercise, what concrete step, if any, does fairness to me or others still require?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:compassionate-reappraisal"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I trying this because I'm ready, or because I feel I ought to have moved on by now?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:compassionate-reappraisal"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "They were wrong to blame me, and I'll correct the record with the manager tomorrow. They were scared of being blamed, which doesn't excuse it, and I hope they learn to own their mistakes. I can wish them that and still watch my back.",
   "wgo:before": "I keep going over every word they said to the manager. They're two-faced, that's all there is to it, and I'll be cold to them from now on.",
   "wgo:situation": "A teammate missed a handover deadline and then told your manager the delay was your fault, and you lie awake replaying it.",
   "wgo:why": "Replaying the offence keeps anger and arousal high, while seeing the person as flawed and in need of change lets the anger ease without denying the wrong or giving up the practical response."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Compassionate reappraisal",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/6"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/7"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Sit somewhere quiet and settle your breathing for a minute or two before you start."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Recall one specific time a particular person hurt or wronged you, and name plainly what they did and what it cost you."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Picture the offender as a whole person with a history, fears and other sides to them, not only as the author of this act."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Treat the wrong as a sign that this person needs to grow or change, without telling yourself it was acceptable."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Try, for about two minutes, to sincerely wish them something good, such as healing or becoming someone who would not do this again."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Notice your thoughts, feelings and body as you do this, and repeat the exercise when you catch yourself replaying the hurt."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/7",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 7,
   "schema:text": "Decide separately, on the facts, what boundary, conversation or accountability the situation still needs."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "If nothing changed tomorrow, would my life be enough, and what exactly would be missing?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:contentment"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is this want mine, or did a comparison or an advert just switch it on?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:contentment"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I confused being content with giving up on something that genuinely needs fixing?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:contentment"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "When I last got what I wanted, how long did the satisfaction actually last?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:contentment"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "Is anything about my work actually worse than it was yesterday? If there's something I really want, like the scope or the pay, I'll go after that on purpose. If not, I'll let the comparison pass.",
   "wgo:before": "I need to start interviewing elsewhere this week; I can't be the one who got left behind.",
   "wgo:situation": "A colleague in a similar role announces a promotion and a bigger title, and your own job, which you liked yesterday, suddenly feels small.",
   "wgo:why": "Contentment separates a real, specific need from wanting that was switched on by comparison; it keeps ambition but stops it from setting the price of one's peace."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/courage/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What exactly am I afraid of losing here, and is that fear in proportion to the real stakes?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:courage"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/courage/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is the cause worth the risk I am about to take, or am I mainly after looking brave?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:courage"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/courage/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "If I stay silent, is that a judgment about timing, or am I just avoiding discomfort?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:courage"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/courage/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I prepared, framed and planned the follow-up, or am I acting on a surge of anger?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:courage"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/courage/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "Ask for two minutes, lay out the test data and what it implies for the date, frame it as protecting the launch the director cares about, and follow up privately afterwards.",
   "wgo:before": "Stay quiet now and let the slip speak for itself later; or blurt out, in front of everyone, that the plan is fantasy.",
   "wgo:situation": "In a planning meeting, a senior director presents a launch date that you know the test results cannot support. Everyone else is nodding.",
   "wgo:why": "Silence avoids risk at the cost of the goal, and a reckless outburst takes risk without judgment. The wiser response accepts a real personal cost for a worthy aim, and uses preparation, framing and follow-up so the risk actually serves that aim."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is this decision actually within my power, and is the outcome really uncertain, or am I deliberating to put off accepting something?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:deliberation"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I checked that the goal itself is a good one, not just how to reach it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:deliberation"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Did I consider more than one way forward before settling on the first idea I had?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:deliberation"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is my confidence here earned by long, well-fed-back experience, or is it just a strong feeling?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:deliberation"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/check/5",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I set a point where thinking stops and acting starts?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:deliberation"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "Is this really my call, and what am I trying to achieve: her success, or a quieter team? Let me list the options, including a coaching plan with a review date, talk it over with HR and her previous lead, and decide by Thursday.",
   "wgo:before": "My gut says she's not cut out for this. I'll announce the move on Monday and be done with it.",
   "wgo:situation": "A manager has to decide within a week whether to move a struggling analyst to a different team or keep coaching her in her current role.",
   "wgo:why": "The wiser response clarifies the goal, widens the options and borrows others' judgment on an important, uncertain matter, but still commits to a decision on time instead of drifting."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Deliberation",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/6"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/7"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Check that the matter is actually up to you and that its outcome is genuinely uncertain; if not, stop deliberating and either accept it or act on what is known."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Say plainly what you are trying to achieve, and ask whether that end is worth pursuing before you plan how to reach it."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "List at least two or three realistic ways of getting there, not just the first one that occurred to you."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "For the most promising option, trace backwards from the goal to the very next thing you would have to do, and drop options whose chain hits something impossible."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "If the decision is important, talk it through with someone who knows this kind of situation."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Before trusting a strong gut feeling, ask whether you have had long, well-fed-back experience with situations like this one."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/7",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 7,
   "schema:text": "Set a point at which deliberation ends, then choose and act promptly, without reopening the question unless new facts appear."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/dichotomy-of-control/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Which part of this situation actually responds to what I decide or do next?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:dichotomy-of-control"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/dichotomy-of-control/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I treating something I could change as if it were fixed, just to avoid acting?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:dichotomy-of-control"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/dichotomy-of-control/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I staking my peace of mind on an outcome that other people or chance will settle?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:dichotomy-of-control"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/dichotomy-of-control/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "The decision isn't mine. What is mine: answering their questions well, briefing my team honestly, and drafting a smaller fallback plan. I'll do those this week and stop checking for news.",
   "wgo:before": "I keep refreshing my inbox and replaying what the committee might think. If they say no, the whole year was wasted.",
   "wgo:situation": "A team lead has submitted a strong proposal for next year's budget and now has to wait three weeks for a committee to decide, while rumours suggest cuts.",
   "wgo:why": "Effort moves to the parts of the situation that respond to it, the outcome is still wanted and planned for, and the waiting no longer decides how the week goes."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Which way do I usually err in situations like this one, too much or too little, and am I correcting for it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:doctrine-of-the-mean"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I calling a choice \"balanced\" just because it sits halfway between two options, rather than because it fits the situation?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:doctrine-of-the-mean"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is the strength of my reaction proportionate to how serious this actually is?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:doctrine-of-the-mean"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I tend to avoid conflict, so I'll lean a little firmer than feels natural: a private conversation, the specific facts, what I need by when, and a real question about what is getting in his way.",
   "wgo:before": "Either I let it slide to keep the peace, or I lay it all out bluntly in front of the team so nobody can say I'm soft.",
   "wgo:situation": "A newly promoted team lead has to tell a long-serving colleague that his reports keep arriving late and incomplete.",
   "wgo:why": "The right degree of firmness depends on this person and this problem, and knowing which way you usually err tells you which way to correct, as Aristotle advised."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emotional-suppression/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I hiding this feeling because the moment calls for it, or because I always hide feelings like this?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:emotional-suppression"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emotional-suppression/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Has the feeling actually changed, or only my face?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:emotional-suppression"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emotional-suppression/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is there someone I could tell how this really landed, and have I told them?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:emotional-suppression"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emotional-suppression/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Could I look at the situation differently, rather than just clamping down on my reaction to it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:emotional-suppression"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emotional-suppression/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "Stay composed in the room, since this isn't the moment, but name it briefly: 'I see it differently; can we go through the data after?' Later, ask what the criticism might be getting right, and talk it over with a trusted peer.",
   "wgo:before": "Keep a blank face, say 'fine', move on, and never mention it to anyone. Feelings have no place at work.",
   "wgo:situation": "In a project review, a senior colleague dismisses your team's proposal in front of everyone. You feel a hot rush of anger and embarrassment.",
   "wgo:why": "Holding back a display for a few minutes can fit the setting; making a rule of never showing or sharing the feeling leaves it running underneath, blurs what you take in, and keeps others from knowing where you stand."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/empathy/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I actually tried to understand how this looks from their side, or am I assuming I already know?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:empathy"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/empathy/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I feeling with them, or am I now caught up in my own distress about their distress?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:empathy"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/empathy/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is my empathy here going only to the person who is closest, most like me or most vivid, while others affected stay invisible?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:empathy"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/empathy/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "After understanding what they feel, what would actually help them, as opposed to what would relieve my discomfort?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:empathy"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/empathy/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I take a minute to really listen and say it back: 'Months of work, and it's gone. That's a real loss.' I notice the heaviness in me, remind myself it is their loss, not mine, and ask what would help. Later I check in and offer a concrete hand with the next project.",
   "wgo:before": "I absorb their upset so fully that I feel sick about it too, then I either pile on about how unfair management is or quietly avoid them for the rest of the week because it is too much.",
   "wgo:situation": "A colleague tells you, close to tears, that their project has been cancelled after months of work, and you have your own deadline in an hour.",
   "wgo:why": "Feeling with someone opens the door, but staying clear about whose feeling it is and turning it into warm concern and practical help keeps you from either drowning in their distress or backing away from it."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emulating-moral-exemplars/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Whose judgment would I trust most in exactly this kind of situation, and what would they notice first?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:emulating-moral-exemplars"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emulating-moral-exemplars/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I copying what my role model did, or what they were trying to achieve?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:emulating-moral-exemplars"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emulating-moral-exemplars/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "When I compare myself with someone better at this, am I working out my next step or looking for reasons to dismiss them?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:emulating-moral-exemplars"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emulating-moral-exemplars/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is the person I'm learning from close enough to my own circumstances that their example is one I can actually follow?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:emulating-moral-exemplars"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emulating-moral-exemplars/check/5",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Are there flaws in my role model I've stopped being willing to see?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:emulating-moral-exemplars"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emulating-moral-exemplars/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "The lead asks the manager how they handled a similar conversation, learns that they always explain the reason in person, acknowledge what the work achieved and offer the person a real role in what comes next, and plans a face-to-face meeting that does those three things in the lead's own words.",
   "wgo:before": "The new lead either copies the senior manager's breezy phrases word for word, or quietly decides that the manager is just naturally charismatic and that there's nothing to learn, and sends a short email.",
   "wgo:situation": "A newly promoted team lead has to tell a long-serving colleague that a project they championed is being cancelled. A senior manager in the next department is known for handling news like this well.",
   "wgo:why": "Emulation borrows the reasoning and the ideal behind an experienced person's choices, not their surface style, and it turns admiration into a concrete step the learner can actually take."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emulating-moral-exemplars/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Emulating moral exemplars",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emulating-moral-exemplars/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emulating-moral-exemplars/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emulating-moral-exemplars/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emulating-moral-exemplars/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emulating-moral-exemplars/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emulating-moral-exemplars/howto/6"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emulating-moral-exemplars/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Pick two or three people whose judgment you trust in a domain that matters to you now (a manager who handles conflict well, a relative who stays fair under pressure), and prefer people close to your own situation over distant heroes."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emulating-moral-exemplars/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Watch for a specific moment where they acted well, and write down what they noticed, what they did and what they chose not to do."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emulating-moral-exemplars/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Ask them, or work out, the reasons behind it, so that you learn the ideal the action served rather than only the gesture."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emulating-moral-exemplars/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "When you feel the sting of falling short, name the specific good you lack and one small step toward it this week, instead of looking for faults in them."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emulating-moral-exemplars/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Try the step in a comparable situation of your own, adapted to your circumstances, then compare the result with what they did and why."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emulating-moral-exemplars/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Widen and update your set of exemplars over time, and drop any you find yourself copying blindly or defending against all criticism."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/equanimity/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I reacting to what actually happened, or to the story I am telling about it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:equanimity"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/equanimity/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is my calm here steadiness, or am I simply refusing to feel or to care?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:equanimity"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/equanimity/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "If this turned out well, or badly, would I still be able to act on my values?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:equanimity"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/equanimity/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What part of this is up to me, and am I putting my energy there?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:equanimity"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/equanimity/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "That hurts, and I'll let myself feel it. What's in my hands now is an honest account of what we learned and what we'll try differently, so that's what I'll present.",
   "wgo:before": "This is a disaster. I'll open with who dropped the ball, and frankly I'm not sure this team can win anything.",
   "wgo:situation": "An hour before you present to leadership, you learn that the client your team spent three months courting has chosen a competitor.",
   "wgo:why": "The loss is still felt, but it no longer chooses your words; attention moves from blame and panic to the part of the situation you can actually shape."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/evening-review/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I reviewing today's conduct to improve it tomorrow, or to punish myself for it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:evening-review"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/evening-review/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I named what went well today, and why, as well as where I fell short?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:evening-review"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/evening-review/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is there one concrete thing I will say or do differently tomorrow as a result of this review?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:evening-review"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/evening-review/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I judging myself by my own considered standards, or by one bad moment?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:evening-review"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/evening-review/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "In a ten-minute review before bed you note that the meeting was otherwise well run, that you interrupted because you were defending a deadline you had promised, and that the concern was valid. You decide to thank the colleague tomorrow and to ask for objections before closing future planning meetings, then put the notebook away.",
   "wgo:before": "You lie awake replaying the moment, call yourself a terrible manager, check your phone to escape the feeling, and the next morning act as if nothing happened.",
   "wgo:situation": "During an afternoon planning meeting you cut off a junior colleague who was raising a scheduling concern, and later in the day the concern turned out to be right.",
   "wgo:why": "A fair, bounded review turns a sting into a specific repair and a better habit, whereas unstructured replay punishes you without changing what happens next."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/evening-review/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Evening review",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/evening-review/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/evening-review/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/evening-review/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/evening-review/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/evening-review/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/evening-review/howto/6"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/evening-review/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Pick a fixed, short slot at the end of the day, such as the last ten minutes before bed, and keep it whether or not the day went well."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/evening-review/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Go through the day in order, recalling what you said and did in the main conversations, decisions and tasks, as if replaying it for a fair observer."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/evening-review/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Ask three questions of each moment that stands out - what did I do well, where did I fall short of my own standards, and what did I leave undone?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/evening-review/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "For each shortfall, name the specific thing you would say or do next time, then let it go as Seneca did, with a pardon rather than a sentence."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/evening-review/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Write down one good thing that happened and why it happened, so the review does not become a list of faults."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/evening-review/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Choose a single intention for tomorrow and, every week or so, look back over your notes for patterns that keep recurring."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Do I actually have the specific knowledge or skill this action needs, or am I borrowing confidence from success somewhere else?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:folly"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Whose interests, besides mine, does this decision affect, and how will it look in a year rather than this week?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:folly"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I assuming the consequences won't reach me because of my position, record or cleverness?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:folly"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "When someone questioned this plan, did I answer their point or just wave it away?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:folly"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "\"Fair question. My experience is with the old schema, not this one, so I don't actually know. Let's run it against the staging copy and ship on Monday, when people are around if it goes wrong.\" The test exposes a locking problem, which is fixed before release.",
   "wgo:before": "\"I've done this kind of change a hundred times. Testing it would take all afternoon, and nothing is going to break.\" The change goes out unreviewed, fails over the weekend, and the on-call staff spend two days repairing it.",
   "wgo:situation": "A senior engineer, the most experienced person on the team, wants to push a database change to the live system late on a Friday. A junior colleague asks whether it has been tested against a copy of the real data.",
   "wgo:why": "Expertise in one area tempts people to feel knowledgeable and safe everywhere; asking what this particular action requires, who bears the cost if it fails, and whether a dissenting question has been answered brings confidence back into line with what is actually known."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/forgiveness/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I holding on to this to protect myself or someone else, or mainly to make them pay?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:forgiveness"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/forgiveness/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I separated forgiving from excusing, forgetting and reconciling, so I know which of these I'm actually being asked to do?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:forgiveness"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/forgiveness/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "If they keep doing this, what boundary would self-respect require alongside any forgiveness?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:forgiveness"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/forgiveness/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I given myself time to name the hurt before deciding whether, and how, to forgive?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:forgiveness"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/forgiveness/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I'll tell them plainly that it was wrong and that I'll put my name on my own work from now on. Then I'll stop rehearsing it and treat them fairly on this project.",
   "wgo:before": "I'll be polite, but I'm keeping score, and I'll make sure the client finds out what they're really like.",
   "wgo:situation": "A colleague presented your analysis as their own to a client, later admitted it and apologised, and you still have to work together on the account.",
   "wgo:why": "Forgiving here means dropping the campaign of payback while keeping the judgement that it was wrong and the safeguards that protect you; it is neither pretending nothing happened nor trusting blindly."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Can I be glad about this person's success, or am I quietly keeping score?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:four-immeasurables"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is what I am calling compassion here help for them, or my own distress at their pain?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:four-immeasurables"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is my calm the steadiness of seeing clearly, or have I simply stopped caring?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:four-immeasurables"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Would I offer this same goodwill to someone I find difficult, or only to people on my side?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:four-immeasurables"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I let the disappointment register, then congratulate my peer properly and mean it. With the teammate I listen and ask what would help, without stoking the grievance, and I accept that the promotion decision is made and no longer mine to change.",
   "wgo:before": "I congratulate the winner through gritted teeth, then spend lunch with the other teammate agreeing that management is hopeless, and leave work feeling worse about both of them.",
   "wgo:situation": "A peer you trained wins the promotion you also applied for, on the same day another teammate tells you their project has just been cancelled.",
   "wgo:why": "Each person needed a different response; sympathetic joy keeps envy from souring the success, compassion meets the setback, and equanimity stops your own loss from colouring both."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "The four immeasurables",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/5"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Name the situation in front of you: someone is doing well, someone is suffering, someone is simply there, or the outcome is out of your hands."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Choose the quality that fits it, goodwill for the ordinary encounter, compassion for suffering, sympathetic joy for another's success and equanimity for what you cannot change."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Check the quality for its look-alike, asking whether goodwill has become clinging, compassion has become your own distress, joy has become excitement or calm has become not caring."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Widen the circle one step, offering the same attitude to someone neutral or difficult, not only to people you already like."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Afterwards, notice which of the four came easily and which you avoided, and practise the neglected one next time."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/gratitude/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I noticed who made this good thing possible, and the effort or intention it took them?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:gratitude"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/gratitude/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I actually told them, specifically, rather than only feeling it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:gratitude"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/gratitude/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is my thanks free, or am I acting out of a sense of debt, guilt or deference I don't really owe?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:gratitude"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/gratitude/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I using \"be grateful\" to talk myself, or someone else, out of a legitimate complaint?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:gratitude"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/gratitude/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I'll tell them specifically what their evening saved, mention it to our manager, and keep an eye out for a chance to help them in turn.",
   "wgo:before": "Good, it's fixed. That's their job anyway; on to the next thing.",
   "wgo:situation": "A teammate quietly stayed late to fix a broken data feed so your quarterly report could go out on time.",
   "wgo:why": "Gratitude notices both the benefit and the goodwill behind it, then answers with thanks and goodwill rather than taking it for granted or treating it as a debt to settle and forget."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/grief-and-loss/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I judging my grief, or someone else's, against a schedule of stages that the evidence does not support?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:grief-and-loss"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/grief-and-loss/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I made room both for remembering the person and for the practical and social life I still have to live?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:grief-and-loss"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/grief-and-loss/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Has intense yearning or numbness kept me from functioning most days for many months, so that it is time to talk to a professional?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:grief-and-loss"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/grief-and-loss/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "Grief doesn't run on a timetable. Missing him and getting on with life can both be part of it, so I'll keep the plan and also set aside Sunday evening to look through his letters.",
   "wgo:before": "I'm supposed to be in the sad stage by now. If I can laugh, maybe I didn't love him enough, so I'll cancel the next plan.",
   "wgo:situation": "Two months after her father's death, Dana enjoys a weekend away with friends, then feels guilty and wonders whether she is grieving \"wrong\" because she has not hit a depression stage.",
   "wgo:why": "Research finds no fixed sequence of stages, and moving back and forth between facing the loss and rebuilding daily life is a normal, healthy pattern rather than a sign of loving less."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I treating enjoyment as frivolous, or meaning as a duty, rather than letting each do its own work in my life?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "When I judge whether a choice will make me better off, am I thinking only about how it will feel this week, or also about whether it fits what I value and want to grow into?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I relying on a neat label (pleasure versus meaning) where my actual experience is more mixed?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I'll do one thing purely for enjoyment, like a long lunch with friends, and one thing I care about, like finishing the bookshelf I'm building with my kid, and see how each leaves me feeling on Monday and a month from now.",
   "wgo:before": "Pleasure is shallow; I'll spend the weekend on a self-improvement course so the time counts for something.",
   "wgo:situation": "After a draining quarter, a team lead plans a free weekend and wonders how to spend it to feel restored.",
   "wgo:why": "Research suggests pleasure-seeking and meaning-seeking pay off on different timescales and work best together, so treating one as the \"real\" happiness tends to shortchange the other."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/honesty/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "If the other person later learned everything I know, would they feel I had misled them, even if every word I said was true?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:honesty"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/honesty/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I keeping quiet here out of tact, or out of fear of an awkward moment?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:honesty"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/honesty/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is the kind thing I am about to say also accurate, and is the accurate thing I am about to say also kind?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:honesty"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/honesty/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What am I telling myself about my own part in this that I would not want someone else to check?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:honesty"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/honesty/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "Not for Friday, as things stand. We found a data issue yesterday. I'll have a revised date and options to you by this afternoon.",
   "wgo:before": "We're in good shape. There are a few loose ends, but nothing to worry about.",
   "wgo:situation": "Your manager asks, in front of the team, whether the migration you lead is on track for Friday. It is not; a data problem surfaced yesterday and you have not yet told anyone.",
   "wgo:why": "The first answer contains no outright lie but is built to mislead, and it spends trust the team will need when the slip comes out. The second states the fact plainly, owns the delay, and pairs bad news with a next step."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I dismissing this objection because of its evidence, or because of who raised it and how well things have gone for me lately?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:hubris"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "When did someone last change my mind on something important, and did I make it easy or costly for them?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:hubris"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Who, if anyone, can still stop me from making this decision, and have I given them what they need to do so?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:hubris"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I treating my organisation's success as proof of my own judgment?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:hubris"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "\"My recent wins are a reason to check myself, not to skip the check. Walk me through your demand figures, and let's have finance stress-test both versions before the board sees either.\" The plan is approved a quarter later at a smaller scale, with a review point.",
   "wgo:before": "\"I've called it right every time so far, and the numbers will catch up with the vision. We're not slowing down for a spreadsheet.\" The analyst stops raising concerns, and the plan goes ahead unchanged.",
   "wgo:situation": "A department head has delivered three strong years in a row and been praised in the trade press. A senior analyst warns that a proposed expansion rests on optimistic demand figures.",
   "wgo:why": "Recent success and praise are exactly the conditions under which leaders overpay and overreach; deliberately inviting the dissenting case and an independent check restores the feedback that power tends to cut off."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "When did I last tell my team, in so many words, that I was wrong about something?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:humble-leadership"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Who did the real work on this result, and have the people above me heard their names?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:humble-leadership"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I asking for input because I will use it, or to look open?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:humble-leadership"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Does this situation call for listening and learning, or for a fast, clear decision that I can review with the team later?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:humble-leadership"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I under-estimated testing, and Priya flagged it in March; I should have listened. Here's the revised plan. Priya, can you walk me through how you sized it so I get it right next time?",
   "wgo:before": "The vendors let us down and testing turned out harder than anyone could have predicted. We'll push harder.",
   "wgo:situation": "A project lead's schedule for a product launch slips by three weeks, partly because she under-estimated the testing work, and an analyst on the team had flagged the risk early.",
   "wgo:why": "Owning the error, crediting the person who saw it and asking to learn from her makes it safe for others to raise risks early, and it fixes the estimating method rather than just the date."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Humble leadership",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto/6"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "When you get something wrong or don't know the answer, say so plainly and early, and say what you will do about it."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Name specific contributions by specific people, in their hearing and when reporting upward; say \"we\" for shared wins and \"I\" for your own errors."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Ask the team for feedback on one concrete thing you did, listen without defending, and tell them later what you changed."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Let people with more expertise on a task teach you, in front of others if possible."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Keep making clear decisions; in a crisis or under tight deadlines, act first and invite reflection afterwards."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Check that the humility is believed, not read as a tactic, by keeping your private conduct consistent with what you say in meetings."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/imaginary-future-generations/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Who will live with this decision after I have moved on, and has anyone in the room spoken for them?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:imaginary-future-generations"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/imaginary-future-generations/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "If I were a member of that future group, what would I ask today's decision-makers to protect?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:imaginary-future-generations"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/imaginary-future-generations/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I treating my guess about future people's wishes as a certainty, or as one voice to weigh?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:imaginary-future-generations"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/imaginary-future-generations/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I written down my reasons so that my successors can see and judge them?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:imaginary-future-generations"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/imaginary-future-generations/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "Before deciding, ask two colleagues to speak as the department's staff in 2045: what will they need from us, and what would they say about this cut? Then weigh their case against this year's pressures, and write down why we chose what we chose.",
   "wgo:before": "Cut it. Nobody in this meeting will be here when those apprentices are senior, and we need the money for this year's targets.",
   "wgo:situation": "A department head is drafting next year's budget and is tempted to cut the apprenticeship programme, whose payoff arrives only after the current team has moved on.",
   "wgo:why": "The first response counts only the people present. The second gives the people who will inherit the decision a voice in the room and leaves a record they can judge us by, without pretending that their interests automatically win."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/imaginary-future-generations/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Imaginary future generations",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/imaginary-future-generations/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/imaginary-future-generations/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/imaginary-future-generations/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/imaginary-future-generations/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/imaginary-future-generations/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/imaginary-future-generations/howto/6"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/imaginary-future-generations/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Name the decision and choose a horizon year far enough ahead (often 25–40 years) that most people in the room will no longer be in charge."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/imaginary-future-generations/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Ask one person, or a separate group, to imagine they actually live in that year and to speak as its residents, staff or customers, rather than simply forecasting."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/imaginary-future-generations/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Have the future side describe what the place is like and what they wish today's decision-makers had done, then list their priorities from that standpoint."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/imaginary-future-generations/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Have the present side list its priorities from today's needs, without trying to anticipate the future group."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/imaginary-future-generations/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Bring both sides together to negotiate one shared plan, and record where the future side changed it and where it was overruled and why."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/imaginary-future-generations/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Rotate the role in later sessions so that everyone has spoken for the future at least once, and end by writing down reasons and advice for your successors."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/impermanence/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I treating something that is already changing as if it should stay exactly as it is?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:impermanence"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/impermanence/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "If this difficult situation is temporary, how would I act differently today?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:impermanence"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/impermanence/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is this good thing worth savouring more because it will not last?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:impermanence"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/impermanence/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I using \"nothing lasts\" to avoid caring or committing, rather than to see clearly?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:impermanence"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/impermanence/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "That team was always going to change; people move on, and so will this new setup. I'll thank my old colleague properly, stay in touch, and figure out what this new group needs from me now.",
   "wgo:before": "This was the best team I've ever had and they've wrecked it. I'll keep doing things the old way and wait for it to be put back.",
   "wgo:situation": "A project manager's team is reorganised; her favourite colleague moves to another group and the weekly rhythm she relied on disappears.",
   "wgo:why": "The wiser response grieves what was good without demanding that it stay fixed, and puts energy into the situation as it actually is."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implementation-intentions/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I named the exact moment when I will act, or only the goal I hope to reach?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:implementation-intentions"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implementation-intentions/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What is the cue that usually pulls me off course, and do I have a then-response ready for it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:implementation-intentions"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implementation-intentions/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Do I still endorse this goal, or am I making plans to avoid admitting I no longer want it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:implementation-intentions"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implementation-intentions/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "If I am about to drop the plan, has something genuinely changed, or has the moment of keeping it simply arrived?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:implementation-intentions"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implementation-intentions/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "\"If I notice I'm about to speak while someone else is mid-sentence, then I'll write my point down and wait for them to finish.\" In the meeting, the urge to cut in becomes her cue to reach for the notepad.",
   "wgo:before": "\"I'll just try harder to listen next week.\" In the next tense meeting the resolution is forgotten within minutes, and she cuts in twice.",
   "wgo:situation": "A team lead has decided, for good reasons, to stop interrupting colleagues in meetings, but keeps doing it when a discussion gets heated.",
   "wgo:why": "A general resolution relies on remembering and summoning willpower at exactly the moment emotion is highest. An if-then plan decides in calm advance what the trigger is and what to do, so the situation itself prompts the wiser response."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implementation-intentions/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Implementation intentions",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implementation-intentions/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implementation-intentions/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implementation-intentions/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implementation-intentions/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implementation-intentions/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implementation-intentions/howto/6"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implementation-intentions/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Check that the goal is one you have actually decided on and still endorse; if you are lukewarm about it, deliberate first, because a plan cannot supply commitment you do not have."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implementation-intentions/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Identify the critical moment, either the opportunity to act (a time, a place, a recurring event) or the obstacle that usually derails you (a temptation, a distraction, a feeling)."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implementation-intentions/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Write one plan per cue in the form \"If [specific situation], then I will [specific action]\", making the cue concrete enough that you will recognise it and the action small enough to start at once."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implementation-intentions/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "For your usual obstacle, add a shielding plan, such as \"If I feel the urge to check messages, then I will note it and keep writing until the timer ends.\""
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implementation-intentions/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Say or rehearse the plan a few times so the cue and the response are firmly linked, and remove anything in the setting that competes with it."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implementation-intentions/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Afterwards, review whether the cue appeared and the plan fired; revise the plan if circumstances have genuinely changed, not merely because keeping it felt hard."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implicit-theories-of-wisdom/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "When I call someone wise, am I responding to their judgment and care for others, or mainly to their intelligence, confidence or age?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:implicit-theories-of-wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implicit-theories-of-wisdom/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Whose advice am I about to rely on here, and what picture of wisdom made me choose them?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:implicit-theories-of-wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implicit-theories-of-wisdom/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Would someone raised with a different idea of wisdom see this choice as wise, and what would they weigh that I am leaving out?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:implicit-theories-of-wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-humility/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Which part of my view have I actually checked, and which part am I only sure of?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:intellectual-humility"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-humility/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What evidence or argument would change my mind here, and have I gone looking for it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:intellectual-humility"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-humility/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "When I was shown a mistake just now, did I feel curiosity or did I feel attacked?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:intellectual-humility"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-humility/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I underselling a strength I really do have, out of false modesty or fear of conflict?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:intellectual-humility"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-humility/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "You're right, I didn't test that assumption. Let's rerun it with your figure and see how much the forecast moves. Thanks for catching it.",
   "wgo:before": "The model is fine. The market just shifted; nobody could have seen that coming.",
   "wgo:situation": "In a project review, a colleague points out that the sales forecast you built last month rests on an assumption you never checked.",
   "wgo:why": "Owning the gap, rather than blaming circumstances or brushing it off, fixes the forecast, shows the team that errors can be raised safely, and treats the critic as an ally in getting it right."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/interpersonal-conflict/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I sure I know why the other person acted as they did, or am I filling the gap with the least charitable story?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:interpersonal-conflict"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/interpersonal-conflict/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "How would a neutral friend who wanted the best for both of us describe this argument?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:interpersonal-conflict"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/interpersonal-conflict/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "How am I likely to see this disagreement a year from now?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:interpersonal-conflict"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/interpersonal-conflict/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is there an outcome that meets the main concern on each side, or am I only trying to win?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:interpersonal-conflict"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/interpersonal-conflict/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I'm exhausted and I said it badly. I don't actually know what this has been like for you from a distance. Can we each list what we can realistically give over the next six months and see what a fair split looks like? This arrangement doesn't have to be permanent.",
   "wgo:before": "I'm the one doing everything while you just send money. You clearly don't care, and I'm done asking.",
   "wgo:situation": "Two siblings are arguing about who should take on more of the care for an ageing parent. One lives nearby; the other earns more and lives two hours away. The latest phone call ended with both hanging up angry.",
   "wgo:why": "The wiser response owns its part, admits what it doesn't know about the other person's position, allows that things can change, and looks for an arrangement both can live with instead of a verdict on who is the better child."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/kill-criteria/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Before I started, did I write down what result, by what date, would tell me to stop?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:kill-criteria"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/kill-criteria/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is each criterion concrete enough that someone else could tell whether it has been met?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:kill-criteria"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/kill-criteria/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Now that a criterion has been tripped, is my reason for carrying on new information, or what I have already put in?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:kill-criteria"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/kill-criteria/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I counting my time and effort against the budget, not only the money?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:kill-criteria"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/kill-criteria/check/5",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Who without a stake in the original decision could check this call?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:kill-criteria"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/kill-criteria/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "When we launched I wrote that we'd stop if we weren't at forty orders a day by the end of month three. We're at eighteen. I'll end deliveries next week, sell the van, and put the two most-ordered dishes on the counter menu.",
   "wgo:before": "We've bought the van and trained the drivers, so stopping now would waste all that. Let's push on until the summer and see if word of mouth picks up.",
   "wgo:situation": "A café owner started a weekday lunch-delivery service three months ago, buying a used van and training two drivers. Orders are well below what she hoped and the service loses money every week.",
   "wgo:why": "The first response weighs what has been spent; the second applies a test set before any results came in, when judgment was not yet coloured by investment and pride, and pairs the exit with a next step."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/kill-criteria/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Kill criteria",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/kill-criteria/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/kill-criteria/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/kill-criteria/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/kill-criteria/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/kill-criteria/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/kill-criteria/howto/6"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/kill-criteria/howto/7"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/kill-criteria/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "When you commit to a goal or project, write down two to four signals that would show it is failing, each paired with a date by which you will check it."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/kill-criteria/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Make each signal concrete and, where you can, numeric, such as a minimum level of sales, sign-ups, savings or progress, so that someone else could tell whether it has been met."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/kill-criteria/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Set a budget for the effort as well as the money, counting hours, weekends and favours, because time spent tends to escape the books."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/kill-criteria/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Share the criteria with someone who had no stake in starting the project and ask them to hold you to them, or to make the stop-or-go call themselves."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/kill-criteria/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "On each review date, compare results with the criteria and ask whether, starting from scratch today, you would begin this."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/kill-criteria/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "When a criterion is tripped, treat stopping as the default; continue only if you can write down new information that justifies it, not the cost already sunk."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/kill-criteria/howto/7",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 7,
   "schema:text": "When you stop, record what you learned, give credit for the progress made, and name the next goal the freed time and money will go to."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/know-thyself/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What would someone who knows me well say about me here that I would rather not hear?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:know-thyself"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/know-thyself/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I judging myself by my intentions while others can only see my behaviour?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:know-thyself"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/know-thyself/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I mistaken a confident story about my motives for real knowledge of them?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:know-thyself"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/know-thyself/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I don't experience myself that way, but two people saw the same thing. I'll ask a colleague to watch the next meeting and tell me what they notice.",
   "wgo:before": "That's not me. I know how I come across, and I'm a good listener.",
   "wgo:situation": "After a project review, a manager is told by two team members that her meetings run long because she rarely lets others finish a point.",
   "wgo:why": "Self-views are least reliable on flattering or unflattering traits, so treating others' observations as evidence rather than an attack is how the maxim is actually followed."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/knowing-when-to-quit/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "If I were deciding today from scratch, with no time or money already spent, would I choose to start this?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:knowing-when-to-quit"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/knowing-when-to-quit/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I persisting because the goal is still reachable and worth it, or because quitting would mean admitting I was wrong?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:knowing-when-to-quit"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/knowing-when-to-quit/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What new goal will this time and energy go to if I let this one go?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:knowing-when-to-quit"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/knowing-when-to-quit/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I giving up because this is unattainable, or only because the current stretch is hard?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:knowing-when-to-quit"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/knowing-when-to-quit/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "If we were starting today, would we fund this? No. I'll show the review the adoption numbers and the alternative, propose winding it down by the quarter's end, and move the team onto the reporting backlog everyone keeps asking for.",
   "wgo:before": "We've put too much into this to stop now. One more release and people will come round, so I'll ask for another two developers.",
   "wgo:situation": "A team lead has spent eighteen months on an internal software tool that users keep ignoring; a cheaper commercial product now does the same job, and the next budget review is in a month.",
   "wgo:why": "The wiser response judges the project on what it will deliver from here rather than on what it has already cost, which is the pull behind escalation, and it pairs stopping with a clear next goal, which is where the well-being benefits of letting go appear."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I weighing my colleagues' advice as seriously as I would have before I had authority over them?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:leading-others"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "When nobody objected in that meeting, did I check whether they agreed or just stayed quiet?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:leading-others"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Whose interests does this decision touch beyond the targets I am measured on?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:leading-others"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I still doing the work myself because it is needed, or because it is where I feel competent?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:leading-others"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "Ask the colleague to walk the team through the design and its trade-offs, put the alternative on the table as one option rather than an order, ask who sees risks in either, and agree how the choice will be made and reviewed.",
   "wgo:before": "I'm the lead now, so we'll do it my way. I'll rewrite the plan tonight and hand out the tasks tomorrow.",
   "wgo:situation": "A newly promoted team lead, formerly the team's strongest engineer, sees a colleague's design for a new service and is sure her own approach would be faster to build.",
   "wgo:why": "Relying on title wins compliance at best and silences the people closest to the work; inviting their view and weighing it treats authority as responsibility for the decision rather than a licence to skip other people's knowledge."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I asking what I want from life, or what this situation is asking of me?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:logotherapy"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is there anything left for me to create, experience or stand for here, even if the outcome is out of my hands?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:logotherapy"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I watching myself so closely that it is getting in the way of what I'm trying to do?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:logotherapy"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "The project is gone, but the people I trained and what we learned stay. What do I want to build next, and how do I want to carry this?",
   "wgo:before": "None of it mattered. I'll keep my head down and stop caring about the work.",
   "wgo:situation": "A team's long-running project is cancelled after a reorganisation, and a project lead feels the past year was wasted.",
   "wgo:why": "Looking for meaning in contribution, relationships and chosen attitude, rather than only in outcomes you control, keeps a setback from emptying out the whole effort."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Logotherapy",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/4"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Name one thing you are creating or contributing right now, however small, and who it serves."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Name one experience or person you value that you could give more attention to this week."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "For a hardship you cannot change, decide what stance toward it you want to be able to look back on."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Turn your attention from monitoring yourself to the task or person in front of you."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/major-life-decision/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I treating \"not deciding\" as if it were not itself a choice?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:major-life-decision"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/major-life-decision/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I assuming the person I'll be in ten years wants exactly what I want today?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:major-life-decision"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/major-life-decision/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Which part of this can I learn about before committing, and which part can I only learn by living it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:major-life-decision"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/major-life-decision/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I can't know now what teaching will feel like, and staying is a choice too. I'll test what I can (shadow a class, ask two teachers what surprised them), decide what I'd want to have tried, and set a date.",
   "wgo:before": "I'll wait until I'm sure I'll be happier as a teacher. Until then, staying put is the safe choice.",
   "wgo:situation": "After eight years in a stable accounting job, Priya has an offer to retrain as a teacher at lower pay, and has been going back and forth for months.",
   "wgo:why": "Waiting for a certainty that can't arrive quietly chooses the status quo, which the evidence suggests people over-favour; gathering what is knowable and naming the real reasons is the wiser path."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is what feels missing right now coherence, direction, or a sense that this is worth doing?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:meaning-in-life"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I treating a bad week or a low mood as a verdict on my whole life?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:meaning-in-life"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Would I still judge this pursuit worthwhile if I stopped feeling drawn to it, and would I still care about it if no one else valued it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:meaning-in-life"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "Which part is missing: does the work no longer make sense to me, have I lost direction, or do I doubt it is worth doing? Let me fix the piece I can, starting with who actually relies on what I do.",
   "wgo:before": "None of this matters, so I'll stop caring, coast, and wait until I feel inspired to find my calling.",
   "wgo:situation": "After a reorganisation, an analyst's work is folded into another team and she starts to feel that her job, and her weeks, no longer add up to anything.",
   "wgo:why": "Splitting meaning into coherence, purpose and significance turns a vague sense of emptiness into a specific, workable question, and meaning tends to follow connection and contribution rather than waiting for a revelation."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "If my time were shorter than I assume, would this still be worth my anger or effort?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:memento-mori"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I using the thought of death to clarify what matters, or to feed dread or reckless indulgence?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:memento-mori"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What would I want to have said or done for the people involved here?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:memento-mori"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "If my time were shorter than I assume, this exchange would not be worth another evening. I'll send a short, civil reply tomorrow and spend tonight with the people in the next room.",
   "wgo:before": "I'll send a reply that puts them in their place, then keep going through my inbox until midnight.",
   "wgo:situation": "You have spent a week stewing over a curt email from a colleague and are drafting a sharp reply late in the evening while your family is in the next room.",
   "wgo:why": "Remembering that time is limited and uncertain shifts attention from winning a minor status contest to the relationships and values you would actually want to have served."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Memento mori",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto/6"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Pick a fixed cue for the reflection, such as waking up, a commute, or the last few minutes before sleep."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Bring to mind, concretely and in your own case, that your life will end and that you do not know when."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Look back over the last day or week and ask how you actually spent your time and attention."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Ask what you would regret leaving undone or unsaid, and whom you would think of first."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Choose one concrete action for today that reflects what matters, and let go of one petty grievance or craving."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Return your attention to the task in front of you; if the reflection leaves you more anxious than clear, shorten it or stop."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Did I collect reasons over a few days, or only those that occurred to me in one mood?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:moral-algebra"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Did I weigh the reasons, or just count which column was longer?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:moral-algebra"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is there one reason so important that it should settle this on its own, whatever the rest of the list says?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:moral-algebra"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I using the list to choose, or to talk myself out of something I had already decided to do?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:moral-algebra"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/check/5",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Now that the balance is clear, have I set a time to act on it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:moral-algebra"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I'll keep a Pro and Con page on my phone for the next four days, weigh the reasons on Friday, and see what's left after cancelling the equal ones. If the only big thing on the Con side is my partner's job, that's a conversation to have before I answer, not a line to cancel out.",
   "wgo:before": "It sounds exciting and I hate saying no to leadership. I'll accept in tomorrow's one-to-one and sort out the details later.",
   "wgo:situation": "A project manager is offered a two-year posting to the company's office in another city and has to reply within a week.",
   "wgo:why": "Gathering reasons over several days stops the mood of one meeting from deciding, weighing rather than counting keeps a single heavy reason from being outvoted by trivia, and the final check surfaces the reason that really matters."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Moral algebra",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/6"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/7"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Use the method only for an important choice that is up to you and genuinely two-sided, not for a matter of taste or a change you have already committed to."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Frame one specific option (for example, \"accept the transfer\") and divide a page into two columns headed Pro and Con."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Over three or four days, add a short note to either column whenever a reason occurs to you, instead of trying to list everything in one sitting."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Bring all the reasons into view and give each a rough weight, such as 1 to 3."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Strike out pairs of reasons of equal weight on opposite sides, and let one strong reason cancel two or three weaker ones that together equal it."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Ask whether any single remaining reason is decisive on its own, or whether a reason you never wrote down is the one actually driving you."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/7",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 7,
   "schema:text": "Wait a day or two; if no important new reason appears, decide by the balance and act on it."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-habituation/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What small act this week would be a genuine rung up the ladder for me, rather than a leap or no step at all?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:moral-habituation"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-habituation/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I doing this because it is the right thing to do here, or mainly to look brave, generous or disciplined?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:moral-habituation"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-habituation/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Did I reflect after the last attempt, or am I just repeating it by rote?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:moral-habituation"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-habituation/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Does this kind of action feel easier or more satisfying than it did a month ago, and if not, is the step the right size?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:moral-habituation"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-habituation/check/5",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I sliding past the mean into the opposite fault, such as rashness instead of courage?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:moral-habituation"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-habituation/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "She starts small: this week she asks one clarifying question about scope in her own team's stand-up; next week she proposes a realistic date for a minor task; later she flags a risk to her manager one to one. After each, she jots down what happened and what to tweak, and only takes on the sponsor review once the smaller acts feel natural.",
   "wgo:before": "She reads a book on assertiveness, resolves to be braver, and at the next big review abruptly tells a senior sponsor in front of everyone that the whole plan is unworkable, then retreats into silence for weeks after it goes badly.",
   "wgo:situation": "A project coordinator notices that she agrees in meetings to deadlines she knows are unrealistic, then works late to cover the gap. She wants to become someone who says what she actually thinks.",
   "wgo:why": "Character changes through repeated, well-aimed acts rather than through resolutions or one dramatic leap. Graded practice with reflection builds both the habit and the judgment to use it at the right time and in the right measure."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-habituation/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Moral habituation",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-habituation/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-habituation/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-habituation/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-habituation/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-habituation/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-habituation/howto/6"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-habituation/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Name one virtue you want more of and the concrete situations where you currently fall short of it (for courage, perhaps raising concerns in meetings or declining unreasonable requests)."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-habituation/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "List those situations from mildest to hardest, and pick one at the bottom that is uncomfortable but clearly manageable."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-habituation/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Do the act on purpose, for the reason the virtue cares about, not for show; rehearse it first if it helps."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-habituation/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Afterwards, note what you did, how it felt, and how it landed, and adjust what you will do differently next time."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-habituation/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Repeat at the same level until it feels fairly easy and even satisfying, then move one rung up."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-habituation/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Check periodically with someone whose judgment you trust whether you are hitting the mean or drifting toward its excess, such as rashness or rigidity."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I rehearsing a possible loss in order to prepare and appreciate, or am I just worrying?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:negative-visualization"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "After imagining this loss, did I come back to what I still have and what I can do now?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:negative-visualization"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Which parts of the outcome I fear are actually up to me?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:negative-visualization"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "Once, I'll list what could go wrong in the presentation, prepare for the questions I can foresee, and accept that the reaction isn't fully up to me. And I'll take a minute to picture not having this job at all, then notice what I'd miss.",
   "wgo:before": "I'll keep replaying how badly the presentation could go every night until then, and keep grumbling about this job.",
   "wgo:situation": "Your manager asks you to present to senior leadership next week, and you also have a job you mostly enjoy but have started to complain about.",
   "wgo:why": "A brief, bounded rehearsal turns vague fear into preparation and restores appreciation, whereas dwelling on the worst only adds suffering before anything has happened."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Negative visualization",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/6"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Choose one thing you value and tend to take for granted, such as a relationship, your health, your job or an ordinary comfort."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Remind yourself plainly of its nature, starting small, for example that this mug can break and that the people you love are mortal."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "For a minute or two, imagine concretely what your life would be like without it, or how it might never have come about."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Return to the present and notice that you do still have it; name one way you will use or appreciate it today."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Before a risky plan, list what could go wrong, separate what is up to you from what is not, and prepare for the parts you can influence."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Stop if the exercise turns into dread or repetitive worry, and shorten it or set it aside."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/personal-and-general-wisdom/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I drawing on what I know about life in general here, or on what I actually know about myself in this situation?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:personal-and-general-wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/personal-and-general-wisdom/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "If a friend described this exact problem to me, what would I tell them, and why am I not following that advice now?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:personal-and-general-wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/personal-and-general-wisdom/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What does this setback show me about my own strengths and weaknesses that I would rather not look at?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:personal-and-general-wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/personal-and-general-wisdom/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I calling myself wise about this because I give good advice to others, or because I have handled my own version of it well?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:personal-and-general-wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I imagining how they feel, or how I would feel in their place?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:perspective-taking"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Which of my beliefs about their view have I actually checked with them?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:perspective-taking"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I asked a question I don't already know the answer to?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:perspective-taking"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is there an option that meets what they want as well as what I want?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:perspective-taking"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I sketch what their fortnight probably looked like, note that I'm guessing, then ask privately how the project is going from their side. It turns out a second project landed on them without my knowing; we reprioritise together.",
   "wgo:before": "I decide they've stopped caring, picture how I'd feel if I were slacking, and send a sharp message about accountability.",
   "wgo:situation": "A team lead notices that a usually reliable colleague has missed two deadlines in a row and seems curt in meetings.",
   "wgo:why": "Imagining their side softened my reaction, but only asking told me what was actually going on; taking and getting perspective together led to a fair and workable fix."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Perspective-taking",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/5"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Before you respond, name your own first reading of the situation so you can set it aside for a moment."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Imagine the other person's day, constraints and goals, and ask what they know that you don't and what they want from this."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Write down two or three guesses about how they see it, and mark each one as a guess."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Check the guesses by asking open questions (\"How does this look from where you sit?\") and listen without rebutting."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Revise your reading with what you heard, then decide what to do, looking for an option that serves both of you."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/practical-wisdom/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What is the purpose behind the rule or plan I'm about to apply, and does applying it here actually serve that purpose?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:practical-wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/practical-wisdom/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Which particular features of this situation would an experienced, fair-minded person notice that I'm skating over?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:practical-wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/practical-wisdom/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I using my cleverness to reach a goal I haven't checked is worth reaching?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:practical-wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/practical-wisdom/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Whose interests, including my own, have I weighed, and whose have I quietly left out?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:practical-wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/practical-wisdom/check/5",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I asked someone with more experience of situations like this what they would see?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:practical-wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/practical-wisdom/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "\"The rule exists to keep the books clean and stop sloppy filing, and neither is at stake here. I'll approve it, note the reason on the record, and suggest finance add a hardship clause so the next person isn't left to luck.\"",
   "wgo:before": "Rules are rules. If I make an exception for one person, I'll have to make it for everyone. Rejected.",
   "wgo:situation": "A team lead's policy is that expense claims filed more than 30 days late are rejected. A reliable new hire files a claim six weeks late, after spending a month away dealing with a family emergency.",
   "wgo:why": "Practical wisdom serves the purpose behind a rule rather than its letter, notices what is particular about the case, and still protects fairness by making the reasoning visible and fixing the policy for everyone."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/process-model-of-emotion-regulation/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Can I change this situation, or only how I see it and respond to it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:process-model-of-emotion-regulation"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/process-model-of-emotion-regulation/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I reaching for my usual strategy, or the one that fits this moment?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:process-model-of-emotion-regulation"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/process-model-of-emotion-regulation/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I replaying this or concentrating on it, rather than rethinking it or looking elsewhere?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:process-model-of-emotion-regulation"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/process-model-of-emotion-regulation/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is what I'm doing with this feeling working, or is it time to switch?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:process-model-of-emotion-regulation"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/process-model-of-emotion-regulation/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "On the call, hold back the frustration since it's not the moment. Afterwards, ask the manager whether part of the work can wait until Monday. For the part that can't, look at it as an outsider would (a one-off, not a verdict on my work), then check an hour later whether that's actually settled the feeling or whether I need to talk it through.",
   "wgo:before": "Keep a straight face on the call, then spend the evening replaying the email and resenting it.",
   "wgo:situation": "An employee opens an email, shortly before a client call, saying that a report they wrote has to be redone over the weekend.",
   "wgo:why": "The wiser response uses more than one point in the process (changing the situation where possible, reappraising what can't change, holding back only briefly) and checks whether the strategy is working instead of letting suppression slide into rumination."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/process-model-of-emotion-regulation/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Process model of emotion regulation",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/process-model-of-emotion-regulation/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/process-model-of-emotion-regulation/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/process-model-of-emotion-regulation/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/process-model-of-emotion-regulation/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/process-model-of-emotion-regulation/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/process-model-of-emotion-regulation/howto/6"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/process-model-of-emotion-regulation/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "When a strong feeling starts, name it and ask whether you actually want to change it, and in which direction."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/process-model-of-emotion-regulation/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Ask whether the situation itself can be avoided, chosen differently or changed; if it can, start there."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/process-model-of-emotion-regulation/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "If the situation can't change, decide where to put your attention, and avoid dwelling on what upsets you."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/process-model-of-emotion-regulation/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Rethink what the situation means, for example by looking at it as a detached observer would."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/process-model-of-emotion-regulation/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Treat holding back your expression as a short-term tool for moments that need it, not a default."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/process-model-of-emotion-regulation/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "After a few minutes, check whether the strategy is helping; keep it, switch, or stop."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is there still something I can do about this, or is it time to let the goal go and invest in another?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:regret"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I learning a specific lesson from this regret, or replaying the same scene and blaming myself?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:regret"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Would I speak to a friend with this regret the way I am speaking to myself?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:regret"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Which choice in front of me now am I most likely to regret not making?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:regret"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I did hold back, and I wish I hadn't. What was I afraid of, and is that still true? The next lead role opens in spring, so this month I'll ask my manager for a stretch project and say plainly that I want to be considered.",
   "wgo:before": "I always bottle it. I keep replaying that week and telling myself what an idiot I was, or I insist I have no regrets at all and change the subject.",
   "wgo:situation": "Two years ago you decided not to apply for a team-lead role; a colleague got it and is thriving, and the news of their promotion brings the old decision back.",
   "wgo:why": "The wiser response accepts the regret without self-attack, extracts the lesson and turns it toward an opportunity that is still open, which is when regret is most useful."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regulatory-flexibility/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Does this moment call for showing what I feel, holding it back, or rethinking the situation?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:regulatory-flexibility"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regulatory-flexibility/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I reaching for the strategy I always use, or the one that fits here?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:regulatory-flexibility"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regulatory-flexibility/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is the way I'm handling this feeling actually working, and if not, what else could I try?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:regulatory-flexibility"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regulatory-flexibility/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Do I have at least two different ways to respond when something like this happens?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:regulatory-flexibility"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regulatory-flexibility/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "Stay composed while announcing it, since the team needs steadiness; then say plainly that she is disappointed too, ask how they're taking it, and later talk it through with a peer. If the composure starts to feel brittle, switch to rethinking what the cancellation frees the team to do.",
   "wgo:before": "Whatever I feel, I keep it off my face. That's how I always handle bad news, at work and at home.",
   "wgo:situation": "A manager learns in a one-to-one that her team's project is being cancelled, and has to tell the team in an hour.",
   "wgo:why": "Holding back expression was right for the announcement and wrong as a blanket rule; reading the moment, having more than one response, and checking whether it works is what the research links to better adjustment."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is what I am about to say true, as far as I actually know, or is it a guess or a convenient story?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:right-speech"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Will saying it help them or the situation, or does it mainly serve my comfort, my image or my wish to be right?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:right-speech"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is this the right moment and the right tone for them to be able to hear it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:right-speech"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I holding back something true and useful only because saying it would be awkward for me?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:right-speech"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/check/5",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Did anything I said today divide people, wound someone needlessly or pass on gossip, and is there something I should put right?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:right-speech"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "The analysis is strong. One thing to fix before tomorrow: slide 6 uses last quarter's cost assumption, which finance dropped. Want ten minutes in the morning to swap in the new number? Everything else I'd leave as it is.",
   "wgo:before": "\"Looks great, you'll be fine!\" Or, at 11 pm, a long message listing every weakness you can find, ending with a suggestion to rethink the whole thing.",
   "wgo:situation": "The evening before a colleague presents to senior leadership, they send you their slides and ask, \"Is this ready?\" The analysis is solid, but the cost figure on slide 6 rests on an assumption you know finance has already rejected.",
   "wgo:why": "The first reply is pleasing but untrue and leaves them exposed; the second is true but harsh, badly timed and more about your critique than their success. The wiser reply is true, useful and timed so it can be acted on, and its goodwill is plain."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Right speech",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/6"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/7"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Before saying anything that matters, ask first whether it is true as far as you actually know, and drop it if it is not, however pleasing it would be."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Ask next whether it is beneficial, meaning it will help the listener or the situation rather than only relieve your feelings or win the point."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "If it is true and beneficial but unwelcome, do not swallow it; choose a time when the person can hear it, and plan to say it plainly and gently."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Check your motive and tone, and speak from goodwill rather than irritation, contempt or a wish to look good."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "While you are speaking, notice whether the words are causing needless hurt, and stop, slow down or rephrase if they are."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Afterwards, review the conversation; if your words did harm, admit it to the person or a trusted friend and resolve to do better, and if they went well, note what helped."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/7",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 7,
   "schema:text": "Watch for the four habits the tradition names, lying, divisive talebearing, harsh words and idle chatter, especially in casual talk where they are easiest to miss."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/rumination/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Has this round of thinking produced a new insight or a next step, or am I replaying the same scene?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:rumination"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/rumination/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I asking how to deal with this, or only why it happened and what it says about me?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:rumination"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/rumination/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What would I advise a friend in exactly this position, and can I take that advice tonight?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:rumination"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/rumination/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I tested the fear I keep circling, or only rehearsed it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:rumination"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/rumination/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "\"If a colleague told me this, I'd ask what exactly went wrong and what they'd do next. The last three updates slipped because I waited for complete data. I'll propose a short interim update every Friday and check that works for her.\" Then you put it down for the night.",
   "wgo:before": "\"Why do I always do this? What does she really think of me? I'm probably the weakest person on the team.\" Two hours later you are still replaying the meeting and have decided nothing.",
   "wgo:situation": "In your annual review, your manager says your project updates are often late. That night you cannot stop thinking about it.",
   "wgo:why": "Asking what happened and how to act, from a step back, turns the same worry into a plan, whereas asking why in a self-critical loop keeps the hurt fresh and leaves the problem untouched."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Did I decide what \"good enough\" means before I started comparing, or am I letting each new option move the target?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:satisficing"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is this choice important and hard to undo enough to justify searching for the best, or would a good option serve just as well?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:satisficing"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I set a limit on how many options or how much time I will spend?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:satisficing"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Now that I have chosen, am I still checking what I gave up or what others picked?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:satisficing"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "We need four things: our existing workflows, a single sign-on, an export option and a price under our budget. I'll trial tools from the shortlist IT already approved, adopt the first one that meets all four, and stop shopping once it's in.",
   "wgo:before": "I'll trial every serious tool on the market, build a forty-row comparison sheet and keep reading reviews until I'm sure we have the best one.",
   "wgo:situation": "A team lead has to replace the team's project-tracking tool within a month, and dozens of products are available.",
   "wgo:why": "Fixing the standard before searching turns an endless comparison into a bounded task, and stopping after the choice spares the team the second-guessing that research links to looking for the best."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Satisficing",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/6"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Before you look at any options, write down the few things the choice must achieve and the minimum each must reach; this is your \"good enough\" line."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Decide in advance how much search the choice deserves, such as a number of options, a deadline or a budget of hours, scaled to how much is at stake and how reversible it is."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Look at options one at a time and take the first that clears every line, rather than collecting the whole field to rank."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "If nothing clears the line within your search budget, lower one standard deliberately; if many options clear it at once, raise one, and say which and why."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Once you have chosen, stop comparing; do not keep checking the options you passed up or what others chose."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Keep maximizing-style search for the rare choices where a better option is worth the extra effort and the decision is hard to undo."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/adversity-and-mortality",
   "@type": "skos:ConceptScheme",
   "skos:prefLabel": "Adversity, loss and mortality"
  },
  {
