  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "If I handed this role, team or budget to someone tomorrow, would it be in better or worse shape than when I received it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:stewardship"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Who will live with the consequences of this decision after I have moved on, and have I counted their interests?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:stewardship"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I taking responsibility for this outcome, or quietly protecting my own record?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:stewardship"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I calling it stewardship when I am really keeping control that others should share?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:stewardship"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "Show my director what skipping the work would cost the team that inherits the system, propose a smaller feature set plus the essential fixes, and write a clear handover note either way.",
   "wgo:before": "Ship the features and skip the maintenance. The target is mine; the next team can deal with the debt.",
   "wgo:situation": "An engineering manager can hit this quarter's delivery target by skipping overdue maintenance on a system the team will hand over to another group next year.",
   "wgo:why": "The first response treats the system as a means to one person's quarterly result. The stewardly response treats it as held in trust for its future users and owners, accepts a visible short-term cost, and is honest with the people who set the target."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/teaching-for-wisdom/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "When I explained this to someone, did I only hand over the right answer, or did I ask whose interests are at stake and over what time span?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:teaching-for-wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/teaching-for-wisdom/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Did I let the other person argue a view I disagree with, from that side, before I judged it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:teaching-for-wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/teaching-for-wisdom/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Did I show that I can be wrong, or did I present myself as the one who always knows?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:teaching-for-wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/teaching-for-wisdom/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Which did I reward, the quick and clever answer or the balanced one?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:teaching-for-wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/teaching-for-wisdom/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "The manager has the trainees list everyone affected (both employees, the rest of the team, customers), what each option means this month and next year, and the best case for the person who would lose out. They discuss whether the rule should simply be applied, bent or changed, and the manager describes a time they handled a similar request badly and what they learned.",
   "wgo:before": "The manager explains the leave policy (first to ask gets priority), confirms that the trainees can recite it, and moves on to the next slide.",
   "wgo:situation": "A manager is training new shift supervisors. The case for the day: two staff members both asked for the same holiday weekend off, and only one can be released.",
   "wgo:why": "Knowing the rule is not the same as judging well when it collides with people's real interests; practising that judgment on the job's actual content builds the habit the trainees will need on the floor."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/teaching-for-wisdom/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Teaching for wisdom",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/teaching-for-wisdom/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/teaching-for-wisdom/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/teaching-for-wisdom/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/teaching-for-wisdom/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/teaching-for-wisdom/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/teaching-for-wisdom/howto/6"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/teaching-for-wisdom/howto/7"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/teaching-for-wisdom/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Pick a real dilemma from material you already teach (a historical episode, a case, a customer complaint) in which people's interests genuinely conflict."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/teaching-for-wisdom/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Have learners list whose interests are at stake (their own, other people's, the wider community's) and what each option does to them in the short and the long run."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/teaching-for-wisdom/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Ask each learner to argue the strongest case for a view they reject, from inside that person's position, then to look for a resolution that takes both sides into account."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/teaching-for-wisdom/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Ask them to name the values behind their choice and to judge whether the means are acceptable, not only the result."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/teaching-for-wisdom/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Lay out the three moves open to them (adapt to the situation, change it, or leave it) and have them say which fits best and why."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/teaching-for-wisdom/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Model the habits yourself by saying what you don't know, changing your mind in front of them when given a good reason, and sharing credit."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/teaching-for-wisdom/howto/7",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 7,
   "schema:text": "Grade or praise answers for how well they balance interests and perspectives, then close by asking where a similar choice shows up in learners' own lives."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/three-dimensional-wisdom-model/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I trying to understand what is really going on here, including what I cannot know, or only looking for facts that confirm my first reaction?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:three-dimensional-wisdom-model"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/three-dimensional-wisdom-model/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I looked at this situation, and my own part in it, from at least one other person's point of view?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:three-dimensional-wisdom-model"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/three-dimensional-wisdom-model/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is my response moved by concern for the people affected, or mainly by protecting my ego?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:three-dimensional-wisdom-model"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Seen from far above and years from now, how big is this, really?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:view-from-above"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I using the wider view to act better here, or to stop caring about people who are affected?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:view-from-above"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Which part of this is about my reputation, and which part is about what is right to do?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:view-from-above"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "Picture this from far above: one meeting among millions happening today, which few will remember next year. What matters is the project and how I treat people. I'll sleep on it, then ask my manager what would have made my proposal stronger.",
   "wgo:before": "Everyone saw that. I'm sending this tonight so they know the decision was wrong and I won't be pushed aside.",
   "wgo:situation": "A colleague's proposal is chosen over yours in front of the whole department, and you spend the evening composing a sharp reply-all email.",
   "wgo:why": "Seeing the slight at its real scale lowers the heat of the moment, and coming back down to one useful action keeps the wider view from turning into either revenge or indifference."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "The view from above",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto/6"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Name the specific thing that is gripping you right now, such as a slight, a setback, a rivalry or a wish for praise."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Picture yourself rising slowly above the room, the building and the city until you can see whole countries and the many lives going on in them at once."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Widen the view in time as well, recalling the people who lived before you and those who will come after, few of whom will ever know of this moment."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "From that height, look back at your situation and ask how large it really is, and what part of it actually depends on you."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Come back down deliberately and choose one concrete, decent action for today, so the wider view ends in conduct rather than detachment."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Stop and set the exercise aside if it leaves you feeling that nothing matters, and talk to someone you trust instead."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/weakness-of-will/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I changing my plan because I have learned something new, or only because the moment of keeping it has arrived?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:weakness-of-will"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/weakness-of-will/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "If I asked myself yesterday, when I made this resolution, would I accept the reason I am now giving for dropping it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:weakness-of-will"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/weakness-of-will/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What is the specific cue that usually pulls me off course here, and have I planned what I will do when it appears?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:weakness-of-will"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/weakness-of-will/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I telling myself a story that makes the easier option look like the wiser one?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:weakness-of-will"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/weakness-of-will/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "\"When I sit down at nine, I open the report file before the inbox.\" You close the mail app, work for ninety minutes, and then deal with email in a block you had already scheduled.",
   "wgo:before": "\"I'll just clear these quickly so my head is free, then start the report.\" By lunch the report is untouched, and you tell yourself that answering email was the responsible choice after all.",
   "wgo:situation": "You decided on Sunday, for good reasons, to finish a grant report before answering the week's routine email. On Monday morning the inbox shows forty unread messages.",
   "wgo:why": "The first response quietly rewrites a sound resolution at the moment temptation is strongest. The second decides in advance when and where the better judgment will be acted on, and removes the cue that would trigger the lapse."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wisdom/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I treating how much I know about this as if it were the same as knowing what to do?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wisdom/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What in this situation am I unsure of, and have I admitted it to myself and to others?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wisdom/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Would this choice still look good to me if I judged it by the kind of life I want to live, not only by today's goal?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wisdom/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I know the code well, but not the customers' timelines or the budget. Let me lay out what I'm sure of and what I'm guessing, ask sales and finance what I'm missing, and recommend the option that serves the people who depend on this, not the one I'd enjoy.",
   "wgo:before": "I know this codebase better than anyone, so the answer is obviously a rewrite. No need to hear the others.",
   "wgo:situation": "A team member with deep technical knowledge is asked whether the team should rebuild a struggling product from scratch or keep repairing it.",
   "wgo:why": "Expertise is not yet wisdom; the wiser answer knows the limits of its own knowledge, takes other perspectives in, and aims at the good of everyone affected."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wise-leadership/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Whose interests does this decision touch, and have I weighed them or only the ones I'm measured on?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:wise-leadership"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wise-leadership/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What do I not know here, and have I said so to the people relying on me?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:wise-leadership"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wise-leadership/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is my confidence coming from the facts of this case, or from my position and past success?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:wise-leadership"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wise-leadership/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What will the people who watched me decide this learn about how to decide?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:wise-leadership"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wise-leadership/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "Lay out who is affected (customers, the support team, the company's reputation, the people chasing the target), tell my manager plainly what we know and don't know about the bug, propose shipping without the faulty part, and walk the junior engineer who found it through how I'm weighing it.",
   "wgo:before": "Ship it. The bug is rare, the target is mine, and we'll patch it quietly next sprint.",
   "wgo:situation": "A team lead is told to ship a feature by Friday to hit a quarterly target; testing has found that it occasionally shows one customer's order history to another.",
   "wgo:why": "The wiser response weighs everyone the decision touches rather than one metric, is honest about uncertainty, and uses the moment to build someone else's judgment."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wise-reasoning/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What don't I know about this situation, and how sure am I really about the other person's motives?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:wise-reasoning"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wise-reasoning/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Could I describe the other side's view in words they would accept as fair?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:wise-reasoning"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wise-reasoning/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "How might this look in a month or a year, and what else could happen besides the outcome I fear?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:wise-reasoning"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wise-reasoning/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is there an arrangement that meets the main concerns on both sides, or am I treating any middle ground as losing?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:wise-reasoning"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wise-reasoning/check/5",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Would I reason about this differently if a friend had brought it to me?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:wise-reasoning"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wise-reasoning/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I don't yet know why this was decided or who pushed for it. I'll ask the lead what problem the merger solves, say plainly what I think would be lost, and propose a handover that keeps the parts that work. This may look different in three months.",
   "wgo:before": "They have clearly sidelined me on purpose. I'll tell the team the plan is a mistake and refuse to hand anything over.",
   "wgo:situation": "Your team lead announces that a project you have run for a year will be merged into another group's work. You learn about it in the same meeting as everyone else.",
   "wgo:why": "The wiser response admits what it does not know, takes the other side's reasons seriously, allows that events can still turn several ways, and looks for an arrangement both sides can live with, which are the four elements researchers score."
  },
