    },
    {
     "@id": "wg:meaning-in-life"
    }
   ],
   "skos:definition": "An everyday Japanese word for what makes life feel worth living, and for the felt sense of having it; research treats it as close to eudaimonic well-being. The popular Western \"ikigai\" Venn diagram of passion, skill, need and pay is a recent business-coaching overlay, not the Japanese concept, and claims that ikigai lengthens life outrun the observational evidence.",
