   ],
   "skos:broader": {
    "@id": "wg:intellectual-virtues"
   },
   "skos:definition": "Doing well, in thought and in action, with respect to how to live: knowing or reasonably believing what matters, seeing the limits of what one knows, and using that understanding to judge, advise and act well. Philosophers debate its exact conditions; psychologists describe it as morally grounded metacognition applied to real problems.",
